The set of input forms grouped under Operational Regimes allows 
you to define the various mechanical and thermal loads to which 
the well will be subjected during its lifetime.
 
Use the form Completion & Testing  to specify the type of the 
well and to define mechanical and thermal loads applied between 
completion and shut-in:
- pressure test
- perforation
 
Use the form Production & Injection to define mechanical and 
thermal loads which arise during the normal operational regime 
of the well:
- production
- injection
 
Use the form Extreme Operations to define extreme mechanical 
and thermal loads which arise during exceptional well operations:
- unloading / evacuation
- fracturing / high rate killing
  